An app's theme. `color` set the launcher's background and nothing else: the
theme took the device's own colors, so an app that asked for red drew
its buttons in the wallpaper's. A `color` the program sets is the theme's
primary; with none, the device's colors stand.

The theme is always light, and the bars' icons are dark to match. Edge to
edge by default follows the device's dark mode, which on a dark device drew
white icons over the app's white.

-- m.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    kotlin {
        android(main=true, color="#dc0a2d")
    }
}

ui.window {
    ui.button(text="Catch")
}
